Subject: [PATCH 330/638] v8: import CEF consumer API surface

Add the exact V8 C++ ABI symbols left unresolved after the native cef.library vector bridge succeeded. Every entry exists in Chromium's pinned V8 monolith and continues to resolve lazily through v8.library; no engine objects are added to CEF.

AI_PHASE: v8-library-convergence

AI_STATUS: cef-v8-import-surface-checkpoint

AI_ASSUMPTION: the CEF-specific V8 calls use the same pinned C++ ABI and resolver contract already proven by Chromium

AI_VALIDATION: manifest has no duplicates; all 14 new mangled symbols are defined by out/aros-v8-library/obj/v8/libv8_monolith.a

AI_EVIDENCE: aros-opal-hosted-clean/test-artifacts/-cef-library-20260724/02-native-cef-library-vector-bridge-link.log

AI_LIMITATIONS: generated trampolines and the remaining non-V8 CEF component imports require the next build pass

AI_DECISION_CHAIN:; Chromium ec8ef7281d; AROS f2e058ef51
